From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TOTK Turnip integration <totk-turnip@localhost>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:30:56 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] tu: use two CCUs for A722

Qualcomm gen7_17_0 identifies chip 0x43020100 with 1 MiB GMEM. Its upstream
Linux snapshot topology lists RB_0/RB_1, CCU_0/CCU_1 and two SPs/two USPTPs.
Match the A722 descriptor to that two-CCU topology while preserving chip IDs,
tile alignment, shared memory and register tables. num_sp_cores shares its
storage with num_ccu, so the A722 is also described with two SPs.

With one CCU the Retroid Pocket Duo (A722) reported a burst of UCHE BR_SP
write page faults on every cold start of the TOTK port; with two it reports
none. Other GPUs are unchanged.

Sources: https://github.com/qualcomm-linux/kgsl/blob/gfx-kernel.le.0.0/adreno-gpulist.h ;
https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/adreno_gen7_17_0_snapshot.h
---
 src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
index 7ab1706fd81..1796c683820 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
+++ b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
@@ -1115,7 +1115,7 @@ add_gpus([
     ], A6xxGPUInfo(
         CHIP.A7XX,
         [a7xx_base, a7xx_gen1],
-        num_ccu = 1,
+        num_ccu = 2,
         tile_align_w = 64,
         tile_align_h = 16,
         tile_max_w = 1024,
